# =============================================================================
# repository ignore rules
#
# One rule decides what belongs here: a path is ignored only when the working
# tree can regenerate it, or when it must never leave the machine that wrote it.
# A file git already tracks stays authoritative even where a pattern below
# matches it: docs/openapi.json is generated but reviewed, and `git rm --cached`
# is the only way to change that. The MSW worker further down is generated and
# never committed, so there the pattern below is the only authority.
#
# Read the "Runtime state" section before deleting anything that matches it.
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------

# Every workspace package links its own tree, so the pattern must not be anchored.
node_modules/

# pnpm's store, when it is kept beside the checkout instead of in the global cache.
.pnpm-store/

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------

dist/
dist-demo/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `pnpm mocks:init` writes this into each app's `public/`, never hand-edited. The pattern is
# recursive on purpose: a bare `public/mockServiceWorker.js` is anchored to the repository root and
# matches neither `apps/console/public/` nor `apps/portal/public/`. No copy is committed: the file
# exists only after `pnpm mocks:init`, in each app, and must stay out of git.
**/public/mockServiceWorker.js

# The Traefik route projection is generated state, not source. The static routes.yml stays.
docker/traefik/dynamic/instance-*.yml
docker/traefik/dynamic/restore-gate.yml

# --- Tests, coverage and reports ---------------------------------------------

coverage/

# Vitest 5 keeps blob reports, attachments and the html/json/junit artifacts under one directory.
.vitest/

# Browser-lane artifacts. The Playwright harness is not in the tree yet (docs/phase-3-verification-strategy.md,
# gap 15), but `scripts/clean.mjs` already treats these two names as output, so they are ignored here too.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
logs/

# --- Caches ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Turbo's local cache — one per package as well as at the root.
.turbo/

# Written at the workspace root by `pnpm lint` and `pnpm stylelint`.
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache

# --- Environment files and secrets -------------------------------------------

# Every env file is local; only the templates are versioned, in each package that has one.
.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local overrides of any other config file.
*.local

# Keys and bundles. No such file is tracked today; the rule exists so that the first one generated
# is never the one committed.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks

# --- Runtime state (NOT build output) ----------------------------------------

# `pnpm dev` and `scripts/lib/runtime-dirs.mjs` create these on the host and compose bind-mounts
# them into the API: instances, backups, the age identity, the root key, the Keycloak admin client
# secret, the catalog working tree and the route projection. No rebuild reproduces it and `pnpm
# clean` refuses to touch it, so neither should `git clean`.
temp/

# --- Editors and IDEs --------------------------------------------------------

# Editor state is personal except the extension list, which is what makes a fresh clone usable
# without a setup step. `git status` stays quiet about everything else in `.vscode/`.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

.idea/
*.iml
.fleet/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.history/

# --- Operating system --------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Temporary files and local tooling ---------------------------------------

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# AI coding-agent workspaces. Each tool writes plans, session transcripts and per-machine settings
# into a dot-directory at the repository root; none of it is project source. Whole directories are ignored
.codex/
.claude/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.continue/
.gemini/
.roo/
.kiro/
.openhands/
.specstory/
.codebuddy/
.trae/
.qoder/

# Aider keeps its transcripts and its tag index beside the checkout; the config (`aider.conf.yml`,
# `.aiderignore`) is versioned on purpose, so only the generated files are listed here.
.aider.chat.history.md
.aider.input.history
.aider.tags.cache.v*/

# Legacy Subversion metadata still present in some checkouts of this tree.
.svn/
